    <statement><p>Suppose that
<me>f(x+h)-f(x) = 4 h x^2  -    8 h x  -    1 h^2 x  +    5 h^2  -    5 h^3.</me>
Find <m>f'(x)</m>.</p>
<p><m>f'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4x^{2}+\left(-8\right)x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The definition of the derivative is
<me>f'(x)= \lim_{h\to 0} \frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}</me>
This problem gives us the numerator, <m>f(x+h)-f(x)</m>.  So,</p>
<p><me>f'(x)= \lim_{h\to 0} \frac{4 h x^2  -    8 h x  -    1 h^2 x  +    5 h^2  -    5 h^3}{h} = \lim_{h\to 0} 4 x^2  -    8 x  -    1 h x  +    5 h  -    5 h^2 = 4 x^2 - 8 x</me></p>
</solution>
